  @Description_8ed7e6fc483e = N'OpenAI''s GPT-6.1 mid-tier Terra model, released October 26, 2026 as the successor to GPT-5.6 Terra; it sits below GPT-6.1 Sol in the GPT-6.1 series and is aimed at everyday agentic, coding and writing work, with strong screenshot understanding. 1,050,000-token context (922K max input), 128K max output. Text and image input, text output. Reasoning effort none, low, medium (default), high, xhigh and max (unlike GPT-6.1 Sol, it accepts none). Function calling, structured outputs and streaming supported on Chat Completions, Responses and Batch. Priced at $1/$5 per 1M, cached input $0.05, cache writes $1.25 (30-minute retention) or $2.50 (12-hour) - half of GPT-5.6 Terra and GPT-6.1 Sol. A prompt above 272K input tokens re-rates the whole request at 2x input and cache rates and 1.5x output ($2/$7.50, cached $0.10); that long-context tier is not modelled. Available on the OpenAI API, Amazon Bedrock (openai.gpt-6.1-terra, lifecycle start 2026-10-23) and OpenRouter. Microsoft Foundry availability is not confirmed and not modelled. OpenRouter''s GPT-6.1 Terra Pro is the same model with reasoning mode set to pro, not a separate OpenAI model id, so it is not modelled. Sources: https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6.1-terra ; https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-6-1-terra/'
